Upon the first expiry of timer T3482 when the PDN CONNECTIVITY REQUEST was sent with request type set to "handover of emergency bearer services" in a stand-alone PDN connectivity procedure, the UE shall:

- Inform the upper layers of the failure to establish the emergency bearer;  
- Optionally, initiate a CS emergency call (if not already attempted);  
- Or, trigger other implementation-specific mechanisms (e.g., attempting emergency call via another IP-CAN as per 3GPP TS 24.229);  
- **Do not** detach locally or attempt EPS attach for emergency bearer services at this stage;  
- **Resend** the PDN CONNECTIVITY REQUEST message and reset/restart timer T3482.

This behavior is consistent with Clause 6.5.1.5, which specifies that for "emergency" or "handover of emergency bearer services" request types, the UE shall retry the procedure up to four times (i.e., on the first expiry, it resends and restarts the timer). The procedure is aborted only on the fifth expiry of T3482.

The MME must evaluate the following criteria to conclude that extended protocol configuration options is supported end-to-end for a PDN connection:

- The UE is in NB-S1 mode;  
- The APN requested for the PDN connection is for UAS services;  
- The PDN Type requested is non-IP or Ethernet;  
- OR, the network has indicated support of the extended protocol configuration options IE in the last ATTACH ACCEPT or TRACKING AREA UPDATING ACCEPT message;  
- AND, the network has included the extended protocol configuration options IE in at least one EPS session management message received by the UE for this PDN connection.  

(Refer to Clause 6.6.1.1, 3GPP TS 24.301)
